  "readings": [
   "ignored_by_design counts as handled: a call a player plans as having no effect on the picture (host/player/player.cpp call_plan, P_NO_EFFECT and P_CHECK) is handled by that plan; a call it does not plan is not_handled and holds nothing",
   "the scene-order allowance: a host answer that failed where the guest's succeeded is allowed only under tools/s5/play_report.py's two rules (BeginScene inside a scene, EndScene with no scene open), and only when the rule's count is all of that method's failures",
   "the recorder captures a call when the stream holds its record, read back whole with its arguments; a pointer payload no player reads has no recorder rule (ID3DXConstantTable::GetConstantByName's name, the D3DXSave* paths), so for those the record is the call and its answer",
   "a method a recorded run reaches is held by the production recording alone; a synthetic case holds only a method no recorded run reaches: neither the production recording nor any run of Documentation/receipts/m7-recorded-runs.json `reached` (the runs that reach it now; a name kept from earlier counts is one no registered run reaches now) counted a call of it, so a method another registered run reaches and the production recording does not is not held until a production recording that reaches it is replayed in both hosts. The synthetic streams are made through the real recording device and recorder on tools/s5/tests/rec_harness.c's stand-in runtime (its guest memory, function table and CPU state), not the lifted game",
   "a method with no effect on the picture is held on the count: its omit stream fails only because the recorder counted no call of it, so that both players handle it rests on the positive stream, where each host's category sum (handled plus ignored_by_design) equals the recorder's count with nothing not handled"
  ],
  "ruled": "M7's numerator: a method counts only when the device answers it, the recorder captures it, and both players handle it.",
  "ruling": "Documentation/decisions/2026-10-04-S5-user-rulings-2.md",
