 "what_the_ceiling_and_the_misses_mean": "4107 of 4222 vtable-shaped call sites are unattributed, of which at most 4080 could be d3d9 calls (the rest have a displacement past the widest d3d9 vtable and cannot be), each listed in the private scan receipt (ceiling_sites). The user ruled on 2026-10-09 (Documentation/decisions/2026-10-09-S5-user-rulings.md, item 1) that the methods called by the binary are the methods the scan proves plus what runs observe, the union this denominator counts, not every method the binary could call; the could-call space is handled by enforcing the closed world at run time. So the ceiling and the methods a driven run called that the scan missed are not G5 pass conditions: the M7 row prints both, and Documentation/scripts/check_m7_inputs.py fails a regeneration in which either grew against HEAD's receipt unless instrument_growth names the cause."
